(Owner ruling Q11, 2026-08-29: `auto`/`automatic`, `enable`/`enabled`,
 `disable`/`disabled` are no longer reserved - the parser's "auto error
 catching" stubs were removed, so all six spellings are ordinary
 variable names.)

a number called auto is 1.
a number called automatic is 2.
a number called enable is 3.
a number called enabled is 4.
a number called disable is 5.
a number called disabled is 6.
Print auto.
Print automatic.
Print enable.
Print enabled.
Print disable.
Print disabled.
